1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To illustrate a lady with the coats of arms of her husband is strictly speaking incorrect. The lady uses the arms of her parental family all her life provided she is of a noble family.  Furthermore this coat of arm
2 CONC s is incorrect as it was created in 1720 and belongs to the branch of the family that became Swedish Friherre.  Anna Juliane von Delwig (born von Zoege) was married to a member of a branch of the family that did not become introdu
2 CONC ced at the Swedish House of Nobility and never used the illustrated coats of arms. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The coat of arms for this Estonian branch of the family is that of members of the untitled nobility, picturing only the central shield of the coat of arms of the Swedish Friherre-family.
