1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konstanty_Ludwik_Plater Constantine Ludwig Plater] (1722 - 1778) - Count, Castellan of Trakai from 1770, Voivode of Mstislav (1758-1770), Castellan of Polotsk (1754-1758), Grand Clerk
2 CONC  of Lithuania (1746-1754), Marshal of the Tribunal of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania in 1754, Starosta (the Elder) of Inflanty and Dinaburg. He was the ambassador of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth to Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The heir of the Plater family descended from the knight of the Livonian Order von dem Broele gen. Plater, a branch of Heinrich Plater, a Polonized German magnate and large landowner in the territory of Latgale, Lithuania, and Bela
2 CONC rus of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1737, Constantine Ludwig Plater inherited the city of Kraslava of the Duchy of Zadvina from his father, Count Jan Ludwig Plater, who had begun to build his castle there. Constantine Ludwig intended to make it the center of all 
2 CONC Latgale, moving all administrative institutions there from Dinaburg, and the spiritual capital of the Inflanty Voivodeship by creating the see of the Inflanty bishop there. A papal bull was even received for this, but the first pa
2 CONC rtition of Poland and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania (occupation of lands by the Russian Empire) in 1772 crossed out these plans.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1755-1767, Constantine Ludwig Plater ordered the construction of a market square and a town hall, a magnificent stone Roman Catholic Church of St. Louis (the patron saint of the entire Plater family) in the late Baroque style, 
2 CONC and the Kraslava Palace, which became the primary residence of the Counts Plater. In 1757, the Kraslava Theological Seminary was opened here - Livonia's (now Latvia) first academic educational institution. In 1754, Bishop A. Ostro
2 CONC vsky invited a congregation of priests, founded in Paris in the 17th century by St. Vincent de Paul, to lead the Kraslava Theological Seminary and prepare priests for Latgale and Ruthenia (now Belarus).
2 CONT
2 CONT Konstanty Ludvik Plater only partially completed the construction of the palace in Kraslava. During his lifetime, the Plater palace library contained about 20,000 volumes. Later, a monastery school for orphans and children of poor
2 CONC  parents was located there.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1754, he was awarded the Order of the White Eagle, a Knight of the Order of St. Stanislav, and the Russian Order of St. Alexander Nevsky.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his marriage to Duchess Augusta Oginska, he fathered several children. The eldest children were appointed leadership positions in Trakai. Two eldest sons joined the Order of Malta and achieved high positions.
2 CONT
2 CONT The middle son, Casimir Constantine Plater, married one of the richest brides in Latgale - Baroness Isabella Ludovica Borch.
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest son, August Hyacinth Plater, completed the palace construction in Kraslava in 1791, but now under the influence of the classicism style.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.seligman.org.il/kraslava_history_1.html History of Kraslava]
2 CONT
2 CONT
