2 CONT The Scottish Law Reporter: Continuing Reports ... of Cases Decided in the Court of Session, Court of Justiciary, Court of Teinds, and House of Lords, Volume 18 pg 36-39
2 CONT >>Admiral George Gustavus Lennock  of Broomrigg, Dumfriesshire died on 12th May 1866 leaving deed of appointment and trust disposition settlement dated in October 1856 and along with five codicils annexed to it Recorded in May 186
2 CONC 6. He left   a son George James and a daughter wife of Colonel Walker of Crawfordton, Dumfiresshire.  His wife had predeceased him. By deed of apportionment and trust Admiral Lennock on the narrative of certain provisions in His m
2 CONC arriage-contract, appointed   that of the sum of  20,000, Which hed had power under his marriage-contract to apportion among the children of His marriage, his marriage-contract trustees Should pay to his son George Lennock a sum o
2 CONC f 5,000 as his share and That balance of 15,000 Should be paid to Mrs Walker...
2 CONT
2 CONT >>to my daughter all the said Anne Murray Walker Otherwise ASSIGNEES or her heirs or Shortly after the date of His father's deed apportionment and trust disposition and settlement George James married Elizabeth Leigh Lennock Bloxa
2 CONC m third party to the case...
2 CONT
