2 CONT  1763 metu Krikstijo kudiki Juozapa Plateliu Baznycioj
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://archiwumkresowe.pl/dzieje-dabrowicy-na-wolyniu-oraz-ostatnich-wlascicieli-hrabiow-broel-plater-herbu-wlasnego/
2 CONT
2 CONT Józef Antoni Wilhelm Broel-Plater (13.06.1750 Szatejki) son of Wilhelm Jan and Petronela née Nagórska. After selling the Zajnów estate in 1771, in the same year he purchased Dąbrowice from Michał Brzostowski. He built his residenc
2 CONC e in Worobin. He also owned Pulmy near Wołdawa and Zahorodzie near Krzemieniec. Maltese Commander. In 1776 deputy to the Samogitian Sejm. In 1788 deputy to the Great Sejm. In 1790 he received the Order of Saint Stanislaus, in 1792
2 CONC  the Order of the White Eagle. In Worobin he had a large library and beautiful collections of works of art. He died in Worobin on 2.09.1832. Buried in the mortuary chapel at the cemetery in Dąbrowica. Married to Teresa Abramowicz 
2 CONC (Abrahamowicz) of her own coat of arms vel Jastrzębiec odznaczenia (*1754 – +1826). She was the daughter of Jerzy, starost of Starodub and Marcjanna (Maria) Dernałowicz of the Lubicz coat of arms, and granddaughter, on her father'
2 CONC s side: Andrzej Abramowicz, heir of Worniany and N. Ogińska. It was her second marriage – her first husband was Tadeusz Śliźnia, a land judge of Grodno.
