1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In primary documents available (George) Wilhelm is referred as George at birth and after death, but otherwise known as Wilhelm throughout his life.  
2 CONT
2 CONT All documentation shows including very critical documents refers to both he and https://www.geni.com/people/Colonel-the-Baron-George-Friedrich-Willhelm-von-Pfeiltizer-gen-Frank/6000000020910455560 as full brothers, children of Ern
2 CONC st Johann and Sophia Catharina Amalia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Additionally, Dietrich had a George https://www.geni.com/people/George-von-Pfeilitzer-gen-Franck/6000000085506749825 the same year as  EJ's (George) Wilhelm 
2 CONT
2 CONT With all other solutions ruled out, the final hypothesis remains that the two brothers had the sons close to the same time, both named them George and then EJ deferred to Diet and used the second name Wilhelm for his oldest son.  
2 CONT
2 CONT However when George son of Dietrich died as an infant and  EJ had a second son, the oldest was already known as Wilhelm, so in an absence of a living George of that generation, he named his second son George, who was George all hi
2 CONC s life,
2 CONT
2 CONT It was not uncommon to drop the third name when no longer in a position of confusion and George 2 may have dropped it anyway so as not to be confused with his older brother Wilhelm
